    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d270-a1">

                <pb facs="0320" n="1054" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1054"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 237.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Neill to Señor
                            Candamo.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1895-08-29"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">August 29, 1895</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 56.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister</hi>: I would again respectfully call
                    the attention of your excellency to the many notes from this legation regarding
                    the payment of the long-pending claim of citizens of the United States upon the
                    Government of Peru known as the Hydrographic Commission of the Amazon, and in
                    view of the opening to-morrow (the 30th instant) of the ordinary session of
                    Congress, I would respectfully ask if your excellency will have the claim
                    presented to this Congress for its early consideration.</p>
                <p>I avail myself, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard R. Neill.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
